  data: {
    LLM: "Prioritize suit coverage early. If your first two cards are of different suits, you are already halfway to a 'Primiera' (the namesake hand). Don't bet heavily on 'Numerus' (same suit pairs) because a single Fluxus or a better Primiera will crush you. The 7 and 6 are the most valuable cards for point totalsâ€”if you have them, you can win even if you tie on the hand type.\n\nThe 'Chorus' Bluff: Since a Chorus (4-of-a-kind) is so rare, players often fold when someone bets extremely high early. You can represent a Chorus by being aggressive before the final two cards are dealt. If you can force the 'Chorus' fear into your opponents, you can steal pots even with a weak Numerus.\n\nPositional Vying: In Primiera, the late bidder has a massive advantage. They can see how much the 'Pot' has grown and if others are 'Checking' (suggesting weakness). If you are in late position and hold a 'Maximus' (A-6-7 in one suit), you should almost always raise to 'Flush out' the Primiera holders. You have the point-power to beat them even if they hit their fourth suit.",
    Player: "Prioritize suit coverage early. If your first two cards are of different suits, you are already halfway to a 'Primiera' (the namesake hand). Don't bet heavily on 'Numerus' (same suit pairs) because a single Fluxus or a better Primiera will crush you. The 7 and 6 are the most valuable cards for point totalsâ€”if you have them, you can win even if you tie on the hand type.\n\nThe 'Chorus' Bluff: Since a Chorus (4-of-a-kind) is so rare, players often fold when someone bets extremely high early. You can represent a Chorus by being aggressive before the final two cards are dealt. If you can force the 'Chorus' fear into your opponents, you can steal pots even with a weak Numerus.\n\nPositional Vying: In Primiera, the late bidder has a massive advantage. They can see how much the 'Pot' has grown and if others are 'Checking' (suggesting weakness). If you are in late position and hold a 'Maximus' (A-6-7 in one suit), you should almost always raise to 'Flush out' the Primiera holders. You have the point-power to beat them even if they hit their fourth suit.",
